VALUES ('de2b28c5-a69c-4276-ad5b-18aa83a52f75', 'ALG.13', 2, 'choice', 'Quadratic formula with irrational solutions', 'Which values of $x$ satisfy $3x^2-6x+2=0$?', '["$x=\\frac{3\\pm\\sqrt{3}}{3}$","$x=\\frac{-3\\pm\\sqrt{3}}{3}$","$x=\\frac{6\\pm2\\sqrt{3}}{3}$","$x=6\\pm2\\sqrt{3}$"]', '$x=\frac{3\pm\sqrt{3}}{3}$', NULL, 'Here $a=3,\ b=-6,\ c=2$, so $b^2-4ac=12$. Then $x=\frac{6\pm\sqrt{12}}{6}$, which simplifies to $x=\frac{3\pm\sqrt{3}}{3}$.', 'checked', '{"lint":[],"solve":{"answer":"$x=\\frac{3\\pm\\sqrt{3}}{3}$","agreed":true,"single_answer":true,"aligned":true,"grade_appropriate":true,"error_free":true,"issues":"","work":"x=(6±√(36-24))/6=(6±2√3)/6=(3±√3)/3. (6±2√3)/3 is double this, not equal.","run_id":"claude-code","at":"2026-10-19T07:04:01.395Z"}}', 'ai', NULL, NULL)
