VALUES ('980e28c5-d940-4fea-9b1f-801690bd6e96', 'BA1.02', 3, 'choice', 'Comparing the sides and corners of shapes', 'Ben compares the sides and corners of some shapes. Which of his facts is true?', '["A pentagon has twice as many sides as a triangle.","A hexagon has twice as many sides as a triangle.","A square has twice as many corners as a pentagon.","A triangle has twice as many corners as a square."]', 'A hexagon has twice as many sides as a triangle.', NULL, 'A hexagon has 6 sides and a triangle has 3, and 2 x 3 = 6, so the first sentence is true. The other sentences do not match the real numbers of sides and corners.', 'checked', '{"lint":[],"solve":{"answer":"A hexagon has twice as many sides as a triangle.","agreed":true,"single_answer":true,"aligned":true,"grade_appropriate":true,"error_free":true,"issues":"","work":"Hexagon 6 sides is twice a triangle''s 3. Others false.","run_id":"claude-code","at":"2026-10-19T01:30:24.935Z"}}', 'ai', NULL, NULL)
