VALUES ('913dd88f-e846-40e7-89a0-9cead6748b42', 'BA2.04', 3, 'choice', 'Subtracting three-digit numbers', 'Use each of the digits 1, 3, 4, 6, 7, 8 exactly once to make two three-digit numbers. What is the greatest difference you can make by subtracting the smaller number from the larger?', '["752","732","742","743"]', '742', '876-134', 'Make the larger number as big as possible with the three largest digits: 876. Make the smaller number as small as possible with the three smallest digits: 134. The difference is 876 - 134 = 742.', 'checked', '{"lint":[],"solve":{"answer":"742","agreed":true,"single_answer":true,"aligned":true,"grade_appropriate":true,"error_free":true,"issues":"","work":"Largest 876, smallest 134: 876 - 134 = 742. Hundreds gap at most 8-1 = 7, then tens 7-3 = 4, ones 6-4 = 2.","run_id":"claude-code","at":"2026-10-19T01:32:17.247Z"}}', 'ai', NULL, NULL)
