VALUES ('e7759aae-ac89-4a22-9214-df928ddea7bd', 'BA3.03', 3, 'choice', 'Perimeter of rectangles and squares', 'A rectangle is 10 units long and 6 units wide. A small rectangle 4 units by 3 units is cut out of one corner, so that the shape that is left has square corners and no hole. What is the perimeter of the shape that is left, in units?', '["46","32","18","60"]', '32', '2*(10+6)', 'Cutting a rectangular notch from a corner does not change the distance around: the two new edges together are as long as the two edges that were cut away (4 + 3 each way). So the perimeter is still that of the 10 by 6 rectangle: 10 + 6 + 10 + 6 = 32 units.', 'checked', '{"lint":[],"solve":{"answer":"32","agreed":true,"single_answer":true,"aligned":true,"grade_appropriate":true,"error_free":true,"issues":"","work":"Removing a corner rectangle leaves an L whose edges still add to the full width and height: 2 x (10 + 6) = 32.","run_id":"claude-code","at":"2026-10-19T01:25:25.476Z"}}', 'ai', NULL, NULL)
