VALUES ('228b4aa8-5293-468f-be94-58c147c6fa7d', 'BA3.04', 3, 'choice', 'Order and grouping properties', 'Exactly one equation below is correct. Which one is it?', '["$12 \\times 5 \\times 2 = 12 \\times 5 + 2$","$12 \\times 5 \\times 2 = 12 + 5 \\times 2$","$(12 \\times 5) \\times 2 = 12 \\times (5 \\times 2)$","$12 \\times 5 \\times 2 = 12 \\times 7$"]', '$(12 \times 5) \times 2 = 12 \times (5 \times 2)$', NULL, 'Both sides of $(12 \times 5) \times 2 = 12 \times (5 \times 2)$ are 120: the grouping changes, not the value. The others are false: 12 x 5 + 2 = 62, 12 + 5 x 2 = 22 and 12 x 7 = 84, but 12 x 5 x 2 = 120.', 'checked', '{"lint":[],"solve":{"answer":"$(12 \\times 5) \\times 2 = 12 \\times (5 \\times 2)$","agreed":true,"single_answer":true,"aligned":true,"grade_appropriate":true,"error_free":true,"issues":"","work":"LHS 120. 12 x 7 = 84; 12 + 10 = 22; 60 + 2 = 62; grouping one is true.","run_id":"claude-code","at":"2026-10-19T01:25:25.515Z"}}', 'ai', NULL, NULL)
