VALUES ('a1ab2bb9-3a3a-4103-8fe4-3d7c4e48a1fe', 'BA3.11', 2, 'choice', 'Deciding whether an answer is reasonable', 'Kira says that $9 \times 48 = 4{,}320$. Which sentence is correct?', '["She is wrong, because 9 times 50 is 450 and 4,320 is far too small.","She is wrong, because 9 times 50 is 450 and 4,320 is far too big.","She is right, because 9 times 50 is 4,500, which is close to 4,320.","She is right, because 9 + 48 is 57."]', 'She is wrong, because 9 times 50 is 450 and 4,320 is far too big.', NULL, '48 is about 50, and 9 times 50 is 450. So the answer should be about 450. Kira''s 4,320 is about ten times too big.', 'checked', '{"lint":[],"solve":{"answer":"She is wrong, because 9 times 50 is 450 and 4,320 is far too big.","agreed":true,"single_answer":true,"aligned":true,"grade_appropriate":true,"error_free":true,"issues":"","work":"9 x 50 = 450, so 9 x 48 is about 450; 4,320 is far too big (exact 432).","run_id":"claude-code","at":"2026-10-19T01:27:09.143Z"}}', 'ai', NULL, NULL)
