VALUES ('26873389-1c62-4daf-82de-f6a2557b8943', 'BA5.05', 1, 'numeric', 'Grouping stories (greatest common factor)', 'Tom has 6 red marbles and 9 green marbles. He puts them into bags that are all the same. Every bag has the same number of red marbles and the same number of green marbles, and no marbles are left over. What is the greatest number of bags he can make?', '[]', '3', '3', 'The number of bags must divide both 6 and 9. The greatest such number is 3. Each bag then has 2 red and 3 green marbles.', 'checked', '{"lint":[],"solve":{"answer":"3","agreed":true,"single_answer":true,"aligned":true,"grade_appropriate":true,"error_free":true,"issues":"","work":"gcd(6,9) = 3 bags.","run_id":"claude-code","at":"2026-10-19T01:35:32.467Z"}}', 'ai', NULL, NULL)
