VALUES ('64d91369-a736-449f-adf1-75abb857d3de', 'BA5.05', 1, 'choice', 'Grouping stories (greatest common factor)', 'Lena has 10 pencils and 15 pens. She makes groups that are all the same, with every pencil and every pen used. What is the greatest number of groups she can make?', '["30","25","5","2"]', '5', '5', 'The number of groups must divide both 10 and 15, and the greatest such number is 5. Each group has 2 pencils and 3 pens.', 'checked', '{"lint":[],"solve":{"answer":"5","agreed":true,"single_answer":true,"aligned":true,"grade_appropriate":true,"error_free":true,"issues":"","work":"gcd(10,15) = 5 groups (2 pencils, 3 pens each).","run_id":"claude-code","at":"2026-10-19T01:35:32.467Z"}}', 'ai', NULL, NULL)
