VALUES ('cef01062-2113-4cd0-af54-2efc03d2a5c2', 'BA5.06', 3, 'numeric', 'Fraction stories with several steps', 'A tank is $\frac{2}{5}$ full. After 12 more liters are poured in, it is $\frac{7}{10}$ full. How many liters does the full tank hold?', '[]', '40', '12/(7/10-2/5)', 'The 12 liters are $\frac{7}{10} - \frac{2}{5} = \frac{3}{10}$ of the tank. So $\frac{1}{10}$ is 4 liters and the whole tank is 40 liters.', 'checked', '{"lint":[],"solve":{"answer":"40","agreed":true,"single_answer":true,"aligned":true,"grade_appropriate":true,"error_free":true,"issues":"","work":"7/10 - 2/5 = 3/10 of tank = 12 L; full = 40.","run_id":"claude-code","at":"2026-10-19T01:35:32.506Z"}}', 'ai', NULL, NULL)
