VALUES ('bd435aef-3cc3-4fd9-a40b-b661ec196235', 'NC26.3.ANR.1', 3, 'choice', 'Order numbers', 'Book A is number $3{,}408$, Book B is number $3{,}480$, Book C is number $3{,}048$ and Book D is number $3{,}804$. A librarian lines the books up from the least number to the greatest number. Which book is third in the line?', '["Book A","Book B","Book C","Book D"]', 'Book B', NULL, 'All have 3 thousands. Compare the hundreds: A 4, B 4, C 0, D 8. C is first and D is last. A and B both have 4 hundreds; A has 0 tens and B has 8 tens, so A comes before B. The line is C (3,048), A (3,408), B (3,480), D (3,804). The third book is Book B.', 'checked', '{"lint":[],"solve":{"answer":"Book B","agreed":true,"single_answer":true,"aligned":true,"grade_appropriate":true,"error_free":true,"issues":"","work":"Least to greatest: C 3,048; A 3,408; B 3,480; D 3,804. Third is Book B.","run_id":"claude-code","at":"2026-10-17T19:22:04.066Z"}}', 'ai', NULL, NULL)
