VALUES ('2cf6f901-cbcb-4f9c-b307-9bf634b6240e', 'NC26.3.ANR.3', 1, 'choice', 'Equal groups and multiplication sentences', 'Maya puts 3 marbles in each of 5 cups. Which number sentence shows how many marbles she has in all?', '["$5 \\times 3 = 15$","$5 + 3 = 8$","$5 - 3 = 2$","$3 \\times 3 = 9$"]', '$5 \times 3 = 15$', NULL, 'There are 5 cups with 3 marbles in each cup, which is 5 groups of 3. Equal groups are found by multiplying, so $5 \times 3 = 15$.', 'checked', '{"lint":[],"solve":{"answer":"$5 \\times 3 = 15$","agreed":true,"single_answer":true,"aligned":true,"grade_appropriate":true,"error_free":true,"issues":"","work":"5 cups, 3 marbles each: 5 groups of 3 = 5 x 3 = 15. Other options give 8, 2, 9 and do not model equal groups of 5 cups.","run_id":"claude-code","at":"2026-10-17T19:20:12.112Z"}}', 'ai', NULL, NULL)
