VALUES ('ff4979b4-76da-4b7c-8781-ebf4b0e2cbfc', 'NC26.3.ANR.5', 3, 'choice', 'Instant recall: 0s, 1s, 2s, 5s and 10s', 'Which equation is true for any whole number $n$ greater than 0?', '["$n \\times 0 = n$","$n \\div 1 = 1$","$0 \\div n = n$","$n \\times 1 = n$"]', '$n \times 1 = n$', NULL, 'Multiplying by 1 leaves a number unchanged. The others are false: $n \times 0 = 0$, $n \div 1 = n$ and $0 \div n = 0$.', 'checked', '{"lint":[],"solve":{"answer":"$n \\times 1 = n$","agreed":true,"single_answer":true,"aligned":true,"grade_appropriate":true,"error_free":true,"issues":"Minor: a property stated for any whole number n is somewhat abstract for Grade 3, but the reasoning (1s and 0s rules) is on-standard.","work":"n x 1 = n always. n / 1 = n (not 1 unless n = 1); 0 / n = 0 (not n); n x 0 = 0 (not n).","run_id":"claude-code","at":"2026-10-17T19:20:12.151Z"}}', 'ai', NULL, NULL)
