VALUES ('8274afdc-0d72-4fe6-b859-d160678670c8', 'NC26.4.ANR.7', 3, 'numeric', 'Find a later term of a pattern', 'A bus has 6 passengers after its first stop. At each later stop, 5 more people get on and nobody gets off. How many passengers are on the bus after its 10th stop?', '[]', '51', '6+5*9', 'After the 1st stop there are 6 passengers. Stops 2 to 10 are 9 more stops, each adding 5 people. 5 x 9 = 45, and 6 + 45 = 51.', 'checked', '{"lint":[],"solve":{"answer":"51","agreed":true,"single_answer":true,"aligned":true,"grade_appropriate":true,"error_free":true,"issues":"","work":"After stop 1: 6. Stops 2 to 10 are 9 more stops, each +5: 6 + 45 = 51.","run_id":"claude-code","at":"2026-10-17T19:20:19.061Z"}}', 'ai', NULL, NULL)
