VALUES ('8f6f69fa-28a7-49d3-8e03-f204e7dd9773', 'NC26.4.SGMR.2', 2, 'numeric', 'Classify a triangle by its sides', 'Here are the side lengths, in centimeters, of five triangles. A: 5, 5, 5. B: 4, 6, 8. C: 7, 7, 3. D: 6, 6, 6. E: 5, 9, 12. How many of the triangles are scalene?', '[]', '2', NULL, 'A scalene triangle has three different side lengths. B (4, 6, 8) and E (5, 9, 12) qualify. A, C and D each have equal sides. So the answer is 2.', 'checked', '{"lint":[],"solve":{"answer":"2","agreed":true,"single_answer":true,"aligned":true,"grade_appropriate":true,"error_free":true,"issues":"","work":"A equilateral, B 4/6/8 scalene, C isosceles, D equilateral, E 5/9/12 scalene. Scalene: B, E = 2.","run_id":"claude-code","at":"2026-10-17T19:22:54.972Z"}}', 'ai', NULL, NULL)
