VALUES ('d95f1677-1bfd-4219-b57f-aca719bf1c9e', 'NC26.6.ANR.3', 1, 'choice', 'Reasoning about decimal operations', 'Maria says that $0.4 \times 0.3 = 1.2$. Which explanation shows her mistake?', '["She should have added: $0.4 + 0.3 = 0.7$","The product should be 12, because $4 \\times 3 = 12$","The product should be 0.012, because the factors have three decimal places in all","Both numbers are less than 1, so the product must be less than 1; it is 0.12"]', 'Both numbers are less than 1, so the product must be less than 1; it is 0.12', NULL, '0.4 and 0.3 are both less than 1, so their product is less than 1. $4 \times 3 = 12$ and there are two decimal places in all (one in each factor), so $0.4 \times 0.3 = 0.12$.', 'checked', '{"lint":[],"solve":{"answer":"Both numbers are less than 1, so the product must be less than 1; it is 0.12","agreed":true,"single_answer":true,"aligned":true,"grade_appropriate":true,"error_free":true,"issues":"","work":"0.4 x 0.3 = 0.12 (4 x 3 = 12, two decimal places). Both factors < 1 so product < 1. Option B wrongly counts three decimal places; C gives 12; D changes the operation.","run_id":"claude-code","at":"2026-10-17T20:21:50.263Z"}}', 'ai', NULL, NULL)
