VALUES ('fc25b500-58e8-43f1-a695-d8ead809fb9c', 'NC26.M1.SGMR.2', 1, 'numeric', 'Rigid motions preserve size and shape', 'Triangle $ABC$ has vertices $A(1, 2)$, $B(5, 2)$ and $C(1, 5)$. It is translated 3 units to the right to make triangle $A''B''C''$. What is the length of $A''B''$, in units?', '[]', '4', '5-1', 'A translation keeps every length. $AB$ runs from $x = 1$ to $x = 5$ along $y = 2$, so $AB = 4$, and $A''B'' = 4$.', 'checked', '{"lint":[],"solve":{"answer":"4","agreed":true,"single_answer":true,"aligned":true,"grade_appropriate":true,"error_free":true,"issues":"","work":"AB = 5-1 = 4; translation preserves length.","run_id":"claude-code","at":"2026-10-18T03:39:02.764Z"}}', 'ai', NULL, NULL)
